// The argument of `integer.parse_unsigned` must be a String. An Int is a
// runtime error (spec/05-stdlib.md).
//
// A halting fault halts the program, so a probe holds one, and no `try` is
// around it, because an implementation may make a halting fault catchable
// (spec/README.md, Conformance). The first line is a control: the function
// runs on a valid argument. A consumer that does not have the function fails
// at the control, not at the fault, so a missing function cannot pass this
// probe.

print integer.parse_unsigned("5");
integer.parse_unsigned(5i);
print "unreachable";

// STATUS: error
// CHECK: 5
// COVERS: fault integer_module_non_int parse_unsigned
